  "reason": "RNA-only scvi_n200 singleprofile is the current best configuration (accuracy 0.520, F1 0.498), while image-only ResNet50 is much weaker, so the most promising direction is RNA representation. The key untested design choice is whether multiprofile aggregation improves performance. config_005 extends the best RNA encoder to multiprofile using the simplest aggregation, avgpool, avoiding unnecessary changes to fusion or transformer aggregation. Compared with config_004, it clarifies the effect of multiprofile for the strongest RNA encoder and sets up a clean follow-up comparison with transformer aggregation."
